-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261106~sparky9~0 (2026-11-06)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * ORDER 252c, study item J8: a step after the GRUB language step, shellprocess@languagepacks, adds the packages of
    the language chosen for the new system with the Locale tool (sparky-stereo-locales --add system, chrooted into the
    new system after apt-get update): the spelling, hyphenation and thesaurus dictionaries, the LibreOffice and Firefox
    interfaces, the manual pages, the Tesseract files and the input method engine of that language, when none of them
    is on the system. Nothing is removed. The image already carries the nine required languages, so on the usual
    image the step finds nothing to add; the developer image (English and German) gets the language here.
  * A language that cannot be added (no network, the tool missing, apt failing) does not stop the installation: it is
    said in the installer's log and kept for the new system by the edition's problems engine, with a repair that
    runs the same command, so the first login shows it. If even that cannot be kept, the installation stops with
    the message in the nine languages (LANGPACKS_ERROR).
  * tests/failures.py: the step's contract (host script, 1800 s) and nine cases with stand-ins for chroot and the engine.

